SUMMARY = {
"digital-pr-for-ai-search": "Digital PR for AI search rewards substance: original data, genuine expertise and useful resources, described consistently across every publication. Start with the local and trade outlets your buyers read, keep your brand facts identical everywhere, and measure success by how AI tools describe you, not just by links.",
"does-google-penalize-ai-content": "Google judges content by its value, not its author. AI-assisted pages that are accurate, original and reviewed by people with real expertise are within Google's guidelines; mass-produced pages made to capture searches are not. Keep a human accountable for every page and publish only what you would be proud to put your name on.",
"how-to-update-old-content-for-ai-search": "Updating old content is often the fastest GEO win available. Start with pages that already earn impressions, put the answer first, correct and source every fact, add the questions buyers ask, link it properly and merge what overlaps. Then measure, learn which changes worked, and repeat on the next page.",
"how-to-write-comparison-pages": "A comparison page earns citations by being the fairest, clearest and most current answer to a buyer's choice. Lead with the answer, compare on the criteria that matter, show it in a table, say plainly who each option suits and keep the facts up to date. Honesty about trade-offs is what makes the page worth quoting.",
"reddit-for-ai-search": "Reddit influences AI answers because it captures what real people think. Brands that listen first, answer honestly under their own name and earn genuine recommendations benefit; brands that try to fake it get caught. Treat Reddit as research and community service, and let your website provide the clear answers people end up sharing.",
"topical-authority-for-ai-search": "Topical authority comes from depth, structure and recognition: answering every important question in one subject well, linking those answers together and earning mentions from others in the field. Concentrate on one theme at a time, keep it current, and expand only when the first theme is genuinely complete.",
}
